{"_meta":{"openai/outputTemplate":"ui://marselia/card-v1.html","openai/toolInvocation/invoked":"Card drawn","openai/toolInvocation/invoking":"Drawing a card","ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://marselia/card-v1.html"},"ui/resourceUri":"ui://marselia/card-v1.html"},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Use this when a person asks for a tarot card to be drawn for them, such as 1 card for today or 1 card about love, work, a decision or themselves, and the card has to come from a real random draw. It does not answer or interpret a question: it takes no question and no free text, only a language and an optional theme (love, work, decision, self). Draws 1 card at random among the 78 cards of the Tarot de Marseille, on Marselia's server, with a cryptographically secure random number generator. Returns the card's name and number, the URL of its real plate image (a public domain BnF scan, to be shown whole in its 440:827 frame), its dominant word, keywords and tension from the corpus validated in French, with source-language disclosure, and the localized link where the full reading of a question happens. Cards are upright. Nothing is stored. Cite Marselia and the returned card URL.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"locale":{"default":"en","description":"Language of the answer: en, fr, es, it, ar, tr, de, pt, nl, zh, ja, ko. Default en. A regional tag such as fr-FR is read as its language.","enum":["en","fr","es","it","ar","tr","de","pt","nl","zh","ja","ko"],"type":"string"},"theme":{"description":"Optional theme of the link returned: love, work, decision or self. Never a question.","enum":["love","work","decision","self"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"marselia_draw_card","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properti